                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[u][b]-Quick Review-[/b][/u]\nThe Dungeon Power is a 3d dungeon runner... is that a genre? It's part 3d platformer, part \"Finish the level as fast as possible\".\n\n[u][b]-Detailed breakdown review-[/b][/u]\n[b]Gameplay:[/b] I highly suggest using a controller in this game, the controls are actually pretty solid, at times your character's momentum feels a bit weird, but you can get the hang of it after a while.\n\nI learned pretty quickly that this game (much like other difficult 2d and 3d platformers) have a tendency to frustrate me quickly... but much like well put together 2d platforms: being able to make some type of progress makes all the difference for me.\n\nCareful on loading your game, I accidenly ended up deleting my save file because it doesn't ask confirmation on weather I'd like to delete or not. I was just absentmindedly clicking the save file to load in, and BAM, I lost it.\n\nThankfully once you learn a level in the game, you KNOW that level. So catching back up to my save was remarkably easier then I expected. ..but not salt-less of course.\n\nhttp://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1313685371\n\n[b]Conclusion:[/b] If you still want a bit of a more solid idea for what you're getting yourself into, feel free to watch the video linked at the bottom of this review. In conclusion, I enjoyed the amount of time I spent in game, and it was enough to drive me forward, I'm not necessarily motivated enough to beat the whole game... and I think part of that comes down to style, theme, and polish.\n\nSome people might enjoy playing an indie game like this... other will just get mad, I like to think I'm a bit of a combination of both.\n\n[b]Unscripted Thoughts Video:[/b]\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SNocZemcDLs&feature=youtu.be",
